# --- project additions beyond the Vite defaults above ---

# Build output (Vite's "dist" above covers the default; "build" is here in case
# the output dir is ever changed)
build/

# Testing
coverage/
.nyc_output

# Env files. Vite's "*.local" above already covers .env.local. This one is
# committed on purpose: the Pages build reads it to bake VITE_API_BASE_URL and
# VITE_CARTO_API_KEY into the bundle, and without it the deployed site has no
# API to call and an unkeyed (watermarked) basemap. Both values are
# client-side by nature -- the browser sends them itself, so they are public
# whether or not this file is committed. Never put a server-side secret here.
.env
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production
!.env.production

# package-lock.json is intentionally NOT ignored: `npm ci` in the Pages
# workflow requires it, and actions/setup-node caches against it.
